# An interpolation lifted over `?` at the plain layer (Type System ch. 4, "Field access,
# indexing, interpolation, the topic": interpolation is an application of the
# text-building function to every hole, and an application lifts over a `?` operand,
# giving `nil` when the operand is). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch;
# subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

?Greet: fn ?Text -> ?Text
fn ?Greet ?name = "hello {?name}!"

?Name: fn Nat -> ?Text
fn ?Name 0 = nil
fn ?Name n = ? "n{n}"

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Or (?Greet (?Name 1)), "none"} {Or (?Greet (?Name 0)), "none"}")      # 0
